      "text": "Concentrate shipments from Pilbara lithium operations rose this month as spodumene prices stabilised across the region, according to port data compiled by demo-wire. Volumes recovered after a maintenance window at one of the region's export terminals finished ahead of schedule.\n\nTraders said Q4 settlements for 6% spodumene concentrate have converged in a narrower band than earlier in the year, easing the margin uncertainty that dominated negotiations through the middle of the year. Several producers have kept output guidance unchanged.\n\nAnalysts caution that downstream conversion margins in China remain compressed, and that the pace of demand recovery from cathode makers will decide whether the price floor holds into next quarter. The report is demo content for the mining-brief-agent sample pipeline.",
